//@version=6
// =====================================================================
// MULTI-STRATEGY CONFIRMATION SYSTEM
//
// Four independent reads of the same chart, and a trade only when enough
// of them agree:
//
//   1. BREAKOUT          — close beyond an N-bar range
//   2. TREND             — DI+/DI- direction, gated by ADX strength
//   3. S/R PUSHBACK      — rejection at a confirmed swing pivot
//   4. SUPPLY/DEMAND     — rejection inside a zone left by an impulse move
//
// THE CONFIRMATION RULE IS THE WHOLE POINT
// Any one of these alone fires constantly and most of those fires are
// noise. An entry needs `minConfirmations` agreeing votes AND at least
// one of them must be an EVENT this bar, not merely a state. The trend
// read is a state: it is true for as long as the trend lasts, so a
// system that counted states only would trade the moment two of them
// lined up and never stop. Breakout, S/R pushback and zone pushback are
// events — true on the bar the thing happens and false afterwards.
// Requiring an event means the system waits for something to occur
// rather than for a condition to persist.
//
// WHY THE TREND SLOT IS DI/ADX AND NOT SUPERTREND
// Supertrend was tried here first and it fought the rest of the system.
// It is an ATR trailing band, so it flips on pullbacks — and a retest of
// support inside an uptrend is exactly when the S/R and demand-zone
// entries fire. With `blockOnOpposition` on, the trend slot was vetoing
// the very setups the other three strategies exist to find.
//
// Two things fix that. ADX gates the vote: below `adxFloor` the trend
// slot votes NEITHER way rather than picking a side, so it goes quiet in
// chop instead of casting a coin-flip vote. And `trendCanOppose` is off
// by default, so the trend read can CONFIRM a setup but cannot VETO one.
// DI+/DI- still cross on a deep pullback; with opposition off, that
// costs a confirmation rather than blocking the trade.
//
// WHAT LAGS, AND WHY THAT IS NOT A BUG
// A swing pivot is not confirmed until `pivotRight` bars have printed
// after it. `ta.pivothigh()` therefore returns a value that is already
// shifted back by that many bars, which is exactly right: it means this
// script cannot see a pivot before the chart could have. The cost is
// that S/R levels arrive `pivotRight` bars late. Reducing pivotRight
// makes them arrive sooner and makes more of them false. There is no
// setting that gives you early and correct.
//
// REPAINTING
// Signals are evaluated on bar close (the default; do not enable
// "calc on every tick" unless you accept that DI+/DI- can cross and
// uncross within a bar). The breakout range uses [1] so it excludes the
// live bar — a range that includes the bar being tested moves with
// price and nothing ever breaks it.
//
// ENTRIES ARE LIMIT ORDERS, AND THEY EXPIRE
// A signal places a limit order `entryAtrMult` x ATR from the level that
// justified it — a retest entry, not a chase. Two consequences that are
// easy to get wrong and are handled explicitly below:
//   * If the retest price is not on the correct side of the market the
//     order is NOT placed. A buy limit at or above the market fills
//     immediately at the market, which is the opposite of what a limit
//     order was chosen for.
//   * An unfilled order is cancelled after `orderExpiryBars`. A pending
//     order left alive fills days later in a setup that no longer
//     exists, and that fill is attributed to a signal that has long
//     since been invalidated.
//
// THIS IS A BACKTEST INSTRUMENT
// TradingView fills every limit order that price touches, with no queue,
// no partial fills and no slippage beyond what you configure. Real fills
// are worse. Treat a losing backtest as conclusive and a winning one as
// a reason to go and measure the spread you actually pay.
// =====================================================================

strategy("Multi-Strategy Confirmation",
     overlay              = true,
     initial_capital      = 100000,
     default_qty_type     = strategy.percent_of_equity,
     default_qty_value    = 100,
     pyramiding           = 0,
     calc_on_order_fills  = false,
     process_orders_on_close = true,
     commission_type      = strategy.commission.percent,
     commission_value     = 0.03,
     slippage             = 2)

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ inputs
grpC = "Confirmation"
minConfirmations = input.int(2, "Votes required to enter", minval=1, maxval=4, group=grpC,
     tooltip="How many of the four strategies must agree. 1 disables confirmation entirely.")
blockOnOpposition = input.bool(true, "Block if any strategy opposes", group=grpC,
     tooltip="With this on, a single opposing vote cancels the trade however many agree.")
requireEvent = input.bool(true, "Require at least one fresh trigger", group=grpC,
     tooltip="The trend read is a state and votes for as long as the trend lasts. Without this the system enters on a persisting condition rather than on something happening.")

grpB = "1. Breakout"
useBreakout = input.bool(true, "Enabled", group=grpB)
breakoutLen = input.int(20, "Range lookback (bars)", minval=2, group=grpB)

grpT = "2. Trend (ADX / DMI)"
useTrend = input.bool(true, "Enabled", group=grpT)
diLength = input.int(14, "DI length", minval=1, group=grpT)
adxSmoothing = input.int(14, "ADX smoothing", minval=1, group=grpT)
adxFloor = input.float(20.0, "ADX floor", minval=0.0, step=1.0, group=grpT,
     tooltip="Below this the trend slot abstains instead of picking a side. 20 is the conventional line between trend and chop; raise it to make the trend vote rarer and more meaningful.")
trendCanOppose = input.bool(false, "Trend may veto the other strategies", group=grpT,
     tooltip="Off by default. DI+/DI- cross on deep pullbacks, which is exactly when the pushback strategies fire — letting the trend slot veto there blocks the best setups. Off, it can confirm but never block.")

grpS = "3. S/R Pushback (pivots)"
useSR = input.bool(true, "Enabled", group=grpS)
pivotLeft = input.int(10, "Pivot left bars", minval=1, group=grpS)
pivotRight = input.int(10, "Pivot right bars", minval=1, group=grpS,
     tooltip="Also the lag: a pivot is not confirmed until this many bars have printed after it.")
srTolAtr = input.float(0.5, "Touch tolerance (x ATR)", minval=0.05, step=0.05, group=grpS)

grpZ = "4. Supply / Demand Pushback"
useZones = input.bool(true, "Enabled", group=grpZ)
impulseAtr = input.float(1.5, "Impulse body (x ATR)", minval=0.5, step=0.1, group=grpZ,
     tooltip="A bar whose body exceeds this leaves the bar before it as a zone — the base the move departed from.")
zoneMaxAge = input.int(200, "Zone max age (bars)", minval=10, group=grpZ)
zoneMaxCount = input.int(6, "Zones kept per side", minval=1, maxval=20, group=grpZ)
drawZones = input.bool(true, "Draw zones", group=grpZ)

grpE = "Entry"
entryAtrMult = input.float(0.1, "Limit offset from level (x ATR)", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=grpE,
     tooltip="0.1 sits very tight to the level. Tighter fills more often at a worse price; wider fills less often at a better one.")
orderExpiryBars = input.int(5, "Cancel unfilled order after (bars)", minval=1, group=grpE)

grpR = "Risk"
atrLen = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval=1, group=grpR)
stopAtrMult = input.float(1.5, "Initial stop beyond level (x ATR)", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group=grpR)
breakevenR = input.float(1.0, "Lock breakeven at (R multiple)", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group=grpR)
trailTightness = input.int(2, "Trail tightness after breakeven (1 loose - 5 tight)", minval=1, maxval=5, group=grpR)

grpA = "Webhook alerts"
alertSecret = input.string("", "Ingest secret", group=grpA,
     tooltip="Leave blank if you are not routing to a webhook.")
alertQty = input.int(1, "Quantity to send", minval=1, group=grpA)

// ------------------------------------------------------------------- atr
// ta.atr is Wilder-smoothed. Every distance in this script is expressed in
// it, so changing to a simple mean changes every stop and every offset --
// do not mix the two.
atr = ta.atr(atrLen)
atrOk = not na(atr) and atr > 0

// Tightness is a 1-5 dial because "2.5 x ATR" means nothing until you have
// watched it run. Higher number, tighter trail, more trades stopped early.
trailAtrMult = switch trailTightness
    1 => 3.0
    2 => 2.5
    3 => 2.0
    4 => 1.5
    => 1.0

// ------------------------------------------------------- 1. breakout
// [1] excludes the live bar. Without it the range contains the bar being
// tested, rises with it, and never breaks.
rangeHigh = ta.highest(high, breakoutLen)[1]
rangeLow  = ta.lowest(low, breakoutLen)[1]
brkLong  = useBreakout and not na(rangeHigh) and close > rangeHigh
brkShort = useBreakout and not na(rangeLow)  and close < rangeLow

// ------------------------------------------------------- 2. trend (DMI)
// DI+/DI- give the direction, ADX gives permission to have an opinion at
// all. `trending` is the whole point: with ADX under the floor both votes
// are false, which is an ABSTENTION, not a neutral opinion — the slot adds
// nothing to either side rather than casting a vote the data cannot support.
[diPlus, diMinus, adx] = ta.dmi(diLength, adxSmoothing)
trending   = not na(adx) and adx > adxFloor
trendLong  = useTrend and trending and diPlus > diMinus
trendShort = useTrend and trending and diMinus > diPlus

// --------------------------------------------------- 3. S/R pushback
// Already lagged by pivotRight when it arrives, so referencing it here
// cannot see into the future.
ph = ta.pivothigh(pivotLeft, pivotRight)
pl = ta.pivotlow(pivotLeft, pivotRight)
var float lastPH = na
var float lastPL = na
if not na(ph)
    lastPH := ph
if not na(pl)
    lastPL := pl

srTol = atrOk ? srTolAtr * atr : na
// Long: price traded down into the support level and closed back above it.
// The close condition is what makes it a rejection rather than a breakdown.
srLong  = useSR and not na(lastPL) and not na(srTol) and low  <= lastPL + srTol and close > lastPL
srShort = useSR and not na(lastPH) and not na(srTol) and high >= lastPH - srTol and close < lastPH

// --------------------------------------------- 4. supply / demand zones
// A zone is the base a move departed from: when a bar's body exceeds
// impulseAtr x ATR, the PREVIOUS bar's range becomes the zone. Zones are
// pruned when price closes through them (a zone that failed is not a zone)
// and when they age out.
var array<float> demTop = array.new<float>()
var array<float> demBot = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   demBar = array.new<int>()
var array<float> supTop = array.new<float>()
var array<float> supBot = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   supBar = array.new<int>()
var array<box>   zoneBoxes = array.new<box>()

pushZone(array<float> tops, array<float> bots, array<int> bars, float t, float b, color col) =>
    array.push(tops, t)
    array.push(bots, b)
    array.push(bars, bar_index)
    if array.size(tops) > zoneMaxCount
        array.shift(tops)
        array.shift(bots)
        array.shift(bars)
    if drawZones
        bx = box.new(bar_index - 1, t, bar_index + 20, b,
             border_color=color.new(col, 40), bgcolor=color.new(col, 85))
        array.push(zoneBoxes, bx)
        if array.size(zoneBoxes) > zoneMaxCount * 2
            box.delete(array.shift(zoneBoxes))
    true

body = math.abs(close - open)
isImpulse = atrOk and body > impulseAtr * atr
if useZones and isImpulse and bar_index > 1
    if close > open
        pushZone(demTop, demBot, demBar, high[1], low[1], color.teal)
    else
        pushZone(supTop, supBot, supBar, high[1], low[1], color.maroon)

// Prune: walk backwards so removal does not shift an index we have yet to
// visit. Forward iteration with removal is how half a list gets skipped.
pruneZones(array<float> tops, array<float> bots, array<int> bars, bool isDemand) =>
    if array.size(tops) > 0
        for i = array.size(tops) - 1 to 0
            broken = isDemand ? close < array.get(bots, i) : close > array.get(tops, i)
            stale = bar_index - array.get(bars, i) > zoneMaxAge
            if broken or stale
                array.remove(tops, i)
                array.remove(bots, i)
                array.remove(bars, i)
    true

if useZones
    pruneZones(demTop, demBot, demBar, true)
    pruneZones(supTop, supBot, supBar, false)

// Pushback: the bar traded INTO the zone and closed back OUT of it, on the
// side the zone is supposed to defend. Both halves are needed. Entering
// alone is just price arriving, and a bar that closes inside the zone has
// not rejected anything yet — it is still being decided. Requiring the
// close beyond the far edge is the strict reading and it is the one that
// makes this a rejection rather than an arrival.
//
// How DEEP the bar went is deliberately not tested. Requiring the low to
// stay inside the zone would throw away the strongest signal there is: a
// wick clean through the zone that closes back above it. That is a zone
// holding under maximum pressure, and it should count for more than a
// shallow touch, not be excluded.
//
// The level reported is the edge the entry will sit against: the TOP of a
// demand zone, the BOTTOM of a supply zone. Where several zones qualify,
// the nearest to price wins — the highest demand top, the lowest supply
// bottom — because a distant zone is not what turned this bar.
inDemand = false
float demandLevel = na
if useZones and array.size(demTop) > 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(demTop) - 1
        t = array.get(demTop, i)
        if low <= t and close > t
            inDemand := true
            demandLevel := na(demandLevel) ? t : math.max(demandLevel, t)

inSupply = false
float supplyLevel = na
if useZones and array.size(supTop) > 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(supTop) - 1
        b = array.get(supBot, i)
        if high >= b and close < b
            inSupply := true
            supplyLevel := na(supplyLevel) ? b : math.min(supplyLevel, b)

sdLong  = inDemand
sdShort = inSupply

// ------------------------------------------------------------- votes
longVotes  = (brkLong ? 1 : 0)  + (trendLong ? 1 : 0)  + (srLong ? 1 : 0)  + (sdLong ? 1 : 0)
shortVotes = (brkShort ? 1 : 0) + (trendShort ? 1 : 0) + (srShort ? 1 : 0) + (sdShort ? 1 : 0)

// An event is something that HAPPENED on this bar. The trend read is
// excluded deliberately: it is true for as long as the trend lasts and
// would let the system enter on a condition sitting there unchanged.
longEvent  = brkLong  or srLong  or sdLong
shortEvent = brkShort or srShort or sdShort

// Confirming and opposing are counted separately, because they are not the
// same question. A trend read pointing the other way on a pullback is weak
// evidence against the trade; the same read pointing WITH it is real
// evidence for. Unless trendCanOppose is on, the trend slot appears in the
// vote counts above but not in the opposition counts here.
longOpposition  = (brkLong  ? 1 : 0) + (srLong  ? 1 : 0) + (sdLong  ? 1 : 0) + ((trendCanOppose and trendLong)  ? 1 : 0)
shortOpposition = (brkShort ? 1 : 0) + (srShort ? 1 : 0) + (sdShort ? 1 : 0) + ((trendCanOppose and trendShort) ? 1 : 0)

longOk  = longVotes  >= minConfirmations and (not blockOnOpposition or shortOpposition == 0) and (not requireEvent or longEvent)
shortOk = shortVotes >= minConfirmations and (not blockOnOpposition or longOpposition  == 0) and (not requireEvent or shortEvent)

// The level the trade is measured from. Breakout wins when present because
// it is the most explicit; otherwise the structure that triggered.
longLevel  = brkLong  ? rangeHigh : ((srLong  and not na(lastPL)) ? lastPL : (sdLong  ? demandLevel : na))
shortLevel = brkShort ? rangeLow  : ((srShort and not na(lastPH)) ? lastPH : (sdShort ? supplyLevel : na))

// ------------------------------------------------------------ entries
flat = strategy.position_size == 0
var int pendingSince = na
var string pendingId = na

alertMsg(string action) =>
    '{"secret":"' + alertSecret + '","action":"' + action +
     '","symbol":"{{ticker}}","quantity":' + str.tostring(alertQty) +
     ',"price":"{{close}}","bar_time":"{{time}}","fired_at":"{{timenow}}"}'

var float plannedStop = na

canEnter = flat and na(pendingSince) and atrOk and barstate.isconfirmed

if canEnter and longOk and not na(longLevel)
    limitPrice = longLevel + entryAtrMult * atr
    // A buy limit at or above the market is a market order wearing a
    // limit order's name: it fills instantly at the worse price. Skip it
    // rather than quietly take a fill the setup did not ask for.
    if limitPrice < close
        plannedStop := longLevel - stopAtrMult * atr
        strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, limit=limitPrice, alert_message=alertMsg("buy"))
        pendingSince := bar_index
        pendingId := "L"

if canEnter and shortOk and not na(shortLevel)
    limitPrice = shortLevel - entryAtrMult * atr
    if limitPrice > close
        plannedStop := shortLevel + stopAtrMult * atr
        strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, limit=limitPrice, alert_message=alertMsg("sell"))
        pendingSince := bar_index
        pendingId := "S"

// Expire an unfilled order. Without this it sits in the book and fills in
// some future bar whose setup has nothing to do with the signal.
if not na(pendingSince) and strategy.position_size == 0 and bar_index - pendingSince >= orderExpiryBars
    strategy.cancel(pendingId)
    pendingSince := na
    pendingId := na
    plannedStop := na

if strategy.position_size != 0
    pendingSince := na
    pendingId := na

// ----------------------------------------------------- stop management
var float stopLevel = na
var float entryR = na
var bool beLocked = false
var float runExtreme = na

justOpened = strategy.position_size != 0 and strategy.position_size[1] == 0
if justOpened
    entryPrice = strategy.position_avg_price
    isLong = strategy.position_size > 0
    rawStop = na(plannedStop) ? (isLong ? entryPrice - stopAtrMult * atr : entryPrice + stopAtrMult * atr) : plannedStop
    // A limit order fills at its price OR BETTER. Price gapping through a
    // buy limit can fill the long BELOW its own structural stop, leaving the
    // stop above the entry — which exits instantly and books a loss that
    // looks like the strategy failing and is really an unhandled fill. Clamp
    // to the correct side. math.min keeps a legitimately distant stop where
    // it is and only moves one that ended up on the wrong side.
    stopLevel := isLong ? math.min(rawStop, entryPrice - 0.25 * atr) : math.max(rawStop, entryPrice + 0.25 * atr)
    entryR := math.abs(entryPrice - stopLevel)
    beLocked := false
    runExtreme := isLong ? high : low

if strategy.position_size > 0
    runExtreme := na(runExtreme) ? high : math.max(runExtreme, high)
    entryPrice = strategy.position_avg_price
    if not beLocked and not na(entryR) and entryR > 0 and close >= entryPrice + breakevenR * entryR
        beLocked := true
        stopLevel := entryPrice
    if beLocked and atrOk
        // Trail only ratchets up. A stop that can loosen is not a stop.
        stopLevel := math.max(nz(stopLevel, entryPrice), runExtreme - trailAtrMult * atr)
    if not na(stopLevel)
        strategy.exit("L-x", from_entry="L", stop=stopLevel, alert_message=alertMsg("exit"))

if strategy.position_size < 0
    runExtreme := na(runExtreme) ? low : math.min(runExtreme, low)
    entryPrice = strategy.position_avg_price
    if not beLocked and not na(entryR) and entryR > 0 and close <= entryPrice - breakevenR * entryR
        beLocked := true
        stopLevel := entryPrice
    if beLocked and atrOk
        stopLevel := math.min(nz(stopLevel, entryPrice), runExtreme + trailAtrMult * atr)
    if not na(stopLevel)
        strategy.exit("S-x", from_entry="S", stop=stopLevel, alert_message=alertMsg("exit"))

if strategy.position_size == 0 and strategy.position_size[1] != 0
    stopLevel := na
    entryR := na
    beLocked := false
    runExtreme := na
    plannedStop := na

// -------------------------------------------------------------- plots
plot(useBreakout ? rangeHigh : na, "Range high", color=color.new(color.gray, 40), style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(useBreakout ? rangeLow : na, "Range low", color=color.new(color.gray, 40), style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(useSR ? lastPH : na, "Swing high", color=color.new(color.orange, 30), style=plot.style_circles)
plot(useSR ? lastPL : na, "Swing low", color=color.new(color.blue, 30), style=plot.style_circles)
plot(strategy.position_size != 0 ? stopLevel : na, "Stop", color=beLocked ? color.lime : color.red, style=plot.style_linebr)

plotshape(longOk  and flat, "Long signal",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.teal,   size=size.tiny)
plotshape(shortOk and flat, "Short signal", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.maroon, size=size.tiny)

// A signal whose retest price was already through the market is skipped
// rather than filled at the market. Marked, because a triangle with no
// trade after it and nothing to explain why is how you end up mistrusting
// the whole script.
skippedLong  = canEnter and longOk  and not na(longLevel)  and longLevel  + entryAtrMult * atr >= close
skippedShort = canEnter and shortOk and not na(shortLevel) and shortLevel - entryAtrMult * atr <= close
plotshape(skippedLong or skippedShort, "Signal skipped (no retest room)", shape.xcross,
     location.top, color.new(color.gray, 30), size=size.tiny)

// --------------------------------------------------------- vote table
// Declared at global scope: Pine does not allow a function declaration
// inside a conditional block, and putting this one inside `if
// barstate.islast` is a compile error rather than a subtle bug.
voteCell(table t, int r, string name, bool l, bool s) =>
    table.cell(t, 0, r, name, text_size=size.small, text_color=color.gray)
    table.cell(t, 1, r, l ? "LONG" : s ? "SHORT" : "-", text_size=size.small,
         text_color=l ? color.teal : s ? color.maroon : color.gray)

var table votes = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 6, border_width=1)
if barstate.islast
    table.cell(votes, 0, 0, "Strategy", text_size=size.small, text_color=color.white)
    table.cell(votes, 1, 0, str.tostring(longVotes) + "L / " + str.tostring(shortVotes) + "S",
         text_size=size.small, text_color=color.white)
    voteCell(votes, 1, "Breakout", brkLong, brkShort)
    voteCell(votes, 2, "Trend ADX " + (na(adx) ? "-" : str.tostring(adx, "#.#")), trendLong, trendShort)
    voteCell(votes, 3, "S/R pushback", srLong, srShort)
    voteCell(votes, 4, "Supply/Demand", sdLong, sdShort)
    table.cell(votes, 0, 5, "Need", text_size=size.small, text_color=color.gray)
    table.cell(votes, 1, 5, str.tostring(minConfirmations) + (requireEvent ? " + event" : ""),
         text_size=size.small, text_color=color.gray)
